From b6a3ec8e0f7acb9581666fe8e890fab3eb585252 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <godkiller_nt@hammermaps.de>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 02:18:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Implement Phase B: CHGrunt attack/cover/search via utility AI

Per docs/designs/hybrid-ai-core-phase-b.md:

- dlls/ai_hybrid_core.h/.cpp: AIEnemyMemory + UpdateEnemyMemory()
  (direct-sight-only confidence model, no position storage - the
  engine already tracks that via CBaseMonster::m_vecEnemyLKP),
  AIConfidenceLevel/ClassifyConfidence() with the named thresholds
  from AGENTS_HYBRID_AI.md section 9, AIUtilityContext + ScoreAttack/
  ScoreCover/ScoreSearch, and DecideAction() (scores all three,
  applies hysteresis, updates AIHybridState). All pure and unit
  tested; replaces Phase A's now-superseded UpdateSnapshot().
- dlls/ai_hybrid.h/.cpp + game.h/.cpp: two new tunable CVars
  (ai_hybrid_decision_interval, ai_hybrid_confidence_halflife); debug
  log now also prints confidence.
- dlls/hgrunt.cpp: PrescheduleThink() throttles DecideAction() calls
  via m_flNextAIDecision (runs regardless of ai_hybrid so debug output
  works without flipping the master switch - no behavior impact since
  GetSchedule() only consumes the result when enabled).
  GetSchedule() integration is deliberately narrow: ShouldUseHybridDecision()
  excludes every safety-critical/scripted-feeling state (repel, grenade
  danger, first contact, no-ammo, flinch) so the hybrid layer only ever
  competes for the "plain ongoing combat" choice between attack/cover/
  search, never the ~250-line hand-tuned decision tree's other variety.
  ResolveHybridSchedule() maps to existing schedules only (no new
  SCHED_ENHANCED_* yet) and double-checks engine conditions before
  committing, falling back to nullptr -> original logic otherwise.

Verified: all core tests pass, client.so/vgui.so byte-identical to the
pre-Phase-A baseline (only hl.so differs, as expected). Manual in-game
playtest of live attack/cover/search behavior is still open - see the
design doc's Open Questions, which also records a recommended
multi-grunt test map (c2a5f) found by scanning existing .bsp files for
the exact monster_human_grunt classname.

